# An interval with 2-limb bounds that contains a ball with a 2-limb center (milestone2.md, "One
# enclosure interface", "Midpoint, radius and the conversions", "Ball to interval"): the directed sums
# of two limbs of the center and the radius, add_down_2_2(c, -r) and add_up_2_2(c, r), then the
# selects of interval_add_2 (a bound that the finite core does not return finite is the infinity on
# its side), and the empty set selected by the test of the radius. Each bound is within A |v| + B of
# c -+ r, the constants of the sum, and a bound c -+ r that is exactly zero is returned as zero, by
# the rule of the directed sums. The whole line gives [-inf, +inf], through the same selects. The
# radius is made a 2-limb number by make_2 (the page writes (-r, 0) and (r, 0)), so that no limb is
# added to a literal zero; its guard changes nothing of a radius, a limb of an object. These are the
# values of lower() and upper() of a Ball<T, 2>. Bounded when every member of the ball is at most
# 2^(emax-2) in magnitude, as the sum of two limbs.
kernel:        ball_to_interval_2
input:         c = c0 c1
input:         stored r
output:        zl = zl0 zl1
output:        zu = zu0 zu1
requires:      ball c r
ensures:       interval_of_ball zl zu x x=c,r tight=outward;rel=(2*(1+u)^3*up((1+u)^3)*up(unit(add_2_2)/(1-unit(add_2_2))*(1+u))+2*u^2)*(1+unit(add_2_2))/(1-u);abs=2*(1+u)^2*(1/2*up((1+u)^3)*eta+up((1+u)*((1+u)^2*eta+eta/2)+eta/(2*u)))+eta+(2*(1+u)^3*up((1+u)^3)*up(unit(add_2_2)/(1-unit(add_2_2))*(1+u))+2*u^2)/(1-u)*tiny(add_2_2) exact_lower=zero(c-r) exact_upper=zero(c+r) bounded_when=abs_le(x,-2)
min_precision: 3
source:        the directed sums of two limbs of the center and the radius (Milestone 2 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   proved
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeBallConvert2.v ball_to_interval_2_correct
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the bounds are directed sums made infinite on their side when not finite, and the empty set is selected after an explicit test; interval_of_ball states what comes out for every canonical ball

nr       = neg(r)
(n0, n1) = make_2(nr)
(p0, p1) = make_2(r)
(l0, l1) = add_down_2_2(c0, c1, n0, n1)
(h0, h1) = add_up_2_2(c0, c1, p0, p1)
al       = abs(l0)
fl       = lt(al, const inf)
ah       = abs(h0)
fh       = lt(ah, const inf)
mi       = neg(const inf)
a0       = select(fl, l0, mi)
a1       = select(fl, l1, 0)
b0       = select(fh, h0, const inf)
b1       = select(fh, h1, 0)
ne       = eq(r, r)
zl0      = select(ne, a0, const inf)
zl1      = select(ne, a1, 0)
zu0      = select(ne, b0, mi)
zu1      = select(ne, b1, 0)
